        <p>As every mother and house-keeper knows, it i 4 actual experience that correctly guides her in building up the " indispensable " requirements of the honle she controls. Few articles, indeed, are as indispensable in tbe home as a box of Zam-Buk, which heals the skin drives pain and disease out of the tissues in avv°:" entirely new and better than ever before has IR° accomplished. Zam-Buk has become the favourite healer for bo—t. use, not merely because it is ready for use the morel, it is wanted,but because it so quickly soothes and bead the smarting cut, the burn or scald got during cookir''' and cures so thoroughly a hundred and one distressittg skin affections. The discovery of Zam-Buk is the outcome of notipr; ing and costly experiment along new lines. It its peculiar virtues in the first instance to certain IP-, herbal extracts which it contains, and these virt°,l3o are emphasised by the special manner in which t"ti extracts are blended together. Expensive 1113 f elaborate machinery is needed for the manufacture ° this highly-refined balm, and the various delicate Pi.,,rct ceases in the manufacture are watchfully tended w expert chemists. k, It takes three months to produce a box of Zara-m° Uut the outcome of this skill and patience wonderful herbal substance, which is the la,t %vol." 14 skin dressings and totally different from any ordi°°— salve. Zam-Buk contains none of the rancid animal friti: present in cheap ointments which at best are 1111591., and unreliable and which become useless in a ve short time. 1301" Neither time nor climate can mar the someness and efficacy of Zam-Buk. In Zam-Buk, -tbs- embodied for the first time all the essentials 0' ideal home first-aid and skin-cure. Zam-Buk is without equal for eczema, ulcers,.ba legs, piles, and children's scalp sores, especially 013° worm caught at school. bin/ Zam-Buk gives results more wonder' ul than anyt hitherto attained, and, as the prudent housewife expense and suffering are saved by keepi