        <p>" TRADE " PROTESTS. pel At the annual Conference of the Licer's", Victuallers' Defence League, at Blackpool on igeciti llee day, a protest was made against what was descliuh.4 as the "extortionate taxation " continued ia tcleir year's Budget. The supply of drink at clubs tin hi. existing conditions was objected to in one of the tions passed, and in another the affiliated associat'.° it were strongly advised to resist the attempts flnit' to was alleged, were being made in some localitieebeir coerce approved societies into ceasing to hold t • meetings on licensed premises.</p>
        <p>The Rev. CANON WILLIS seconded, and Mrs. BUCKTON briefly replied. The following were the stallholders :—Glass and china stall, Mrs. Hendy-Cock, assisted by Mrs. Bowden ; sweet stall, Mrs. Darwall ; plain work stall, Miss White and Mrs. Langdale; fancy work stall, Misses E. White and Timewell ; Newton stall, Miss Watkins ; packing stall, Miss S. White. The proceeds amounted to .£lB 15s. 4d., and it is hoped this amount will be increased by donations.</p>
