      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-05-24_WidnesExaminer_art0214" n="art0214">
        <head>BABY ONE MASS OF ECZEMA.</head>
        <p>BABY ONE MASS OF ECZEMA.</p>
        <p>7 -.'</p>
        <p>i I</p>
        <p>Race Horse Cottage, Llanelly Hill, Abergarennn S. Wales.—" I have a little girl gone eight years ow and when a baby five days old eczema started to core°' She was one solid mass from head to foot. I had tO carry her on a pillow for such a time. It started ii her eye and worked round to the ears, neck and bead. and then started on her little back. She had to wear . gloves so that she could not scratch it. She wilt nearly blind for four or five days. " ha eczema was like a little boil and then dfa. charged and then formed a scab, and when it mu%drY and mending it would shell off. I had to make to put on her head so that she could not scratch it. " was so irritating for her and made her so cram dot she could not sleep at all. We were up by night for ' three or four weeks. I first washed her w:th that Cuticura Soap and then put the Cuticnra Ointment oa after, and the ectema was cleared away. She has 14 had anything since. My baby, now ten mantke,. wi_l,ll4 ' very near the same, and she is quite from the eczema by Cuticura Soap and (Signed) - (Signed) Mrs. Alice Aylett, 143brnary let, 1913* Cuticura Soap and Ointment are sold by chemists% everywhere. A sample of each with 32-p. book post-fro° from nearest depot. Address: New bery, 2, Charteroeho ST, London ; R. Towns kt Co. Sydney, N.S- /17' ; Lennon, Ltd., Cape Town; Muller, Maclean de Calcutta and Bombay; or " Cutioura," Boston, 1.7.b.1; Men who shave and shampoo with Cuticura Soap 10A find it best for skin and scalp.</p>
