        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. ROYAL VISIT, 7rn JLTLY, 1913. TENDERS are invited for the DECORATION of the ROUTE along which their Majesties propose to travel. Specification, particulars and plans may be obtained from the undersigned on and after the 2Sth instant, on payment of a deposit of 10s. 6d., which will be returned on receipt of a bona fide Tender. The lowest or any Tender not necessarily accepted. Tenders endorsed " Decorations "to be received by the undersigned not later than noon on Wednesday, the 4th June, 1913. Town Hall, Warrington. J. LYON WHITTLE, 23rd May, 1913. Town Clerk.</p>
        <p>ANCASHIRE COUNTY ASYLUM, WINWICK, WARRINGTON. The COMMITTEE OF VISITORS invite TENDERS for the supply of HOUSE COAL and SLACK from the Ist July, 1913, to the 30th June, 1914. Tenders musf be made on forms which can be obtained from the undersigned, end must be delivered at the Asylum not later than 9 arc, on Wednesday, June 11th. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender, end reserve to themselves the right to accept or reject the whole or part of any Tender. By Order, P. IRVING DUTTON, 19th May, 1913. Clerk and Steward.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. TO PAINTERS AND DECORATORS. The Sites and Buildings Co mmittee of the Education Committee of the Council of the County Borough of Warrington is prepared to receive TENDERS for the PAINTING OF THE VARIOUS SCHOOLS. Specifications, &amp;c., may be seen and forms of tender and all further information obtained at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after Wednesday next, the 28th inst., at which place tenders must be delivered before 12 o'clock noon on Wednes- day, tbe 11th day of June, 1913. A deposit of 10s. 6d. will be required for the Specification, which sum will be returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Cheques to ha made payable to the Borough Treasurer. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted. ANDREW I\l. KER, Borough Engineer and Survsyor. Borough Engineer and Surveyor's Office, Ma y 23rd, 1913.</p>
        <p>FUEL.—The COMMISSIONERS of H.M. WORKS, &amp;c., are prepared to receive TENDERS for the SUPPLY of COAL and COKE to the Government Buildings in the Warrington District, during a period of One Year from the Ist of July, 1913. Forms of Tender, conditions of contract and all particulars may be obtained on application to the Controller of Supplies, H.M. Office of Works, 18, Queen Anne's Gate, Westminster, S.W. Tenders must include for delivery into Cellars. The Commissioners do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any Tender. Tenders must be delivered before 11 B.M. on Friday the 13th June, 1913, addressed to The SECRETARY, H. 11.1 OFFICE OF WORKS, &amp;C., Storey's Gate, London, S.W. and endorsed "Tender for Warrington, Coal and Coke.' H.M. Office of Works, &amp;c. 19th May, 1913.</p>
